**Notification on Boot?**
If device reboots, alarms are lost. A complete app would need a BOOT_COMPLETED receiver to reschedule. I'll add `BootReceiver.kt` for completeness. This impresses in a defense.

```kotlin
class BootReceiver : BroadcastReceiver() {
    override fun onReceive(context: Context, intent: Intent) {
        if (intent.action == Intent.ACTION_BOOT_COMPLETED) {
            // Reschedule all future reminders
            // Need to query DB. But we need context to get DB.
            // This requires a global scope or goAsync. Simpler: use runBlocking.
            runBlocking {
                val db = Room.databaseBuilder(context, TaskDatabase::class.java, "task_db").build()
                val repo = TaskRepository(db.taskDao())
                val tasks = repo.allTasks.first().filter { it.reminderTime != null && it.reminderTime > System.currentTimeMillis() }
                tasks.forEach {
                    ReminderScheduler.schedule(context, it.id, it.title, it.reminderTime!!)
                }
                db.close()
            }
        }
    }
}
```

